content.text:
Usage:

```rust
// Service boundary samples time once per request.
.map(|history| summarize_member(history, CalendarYear::containing(Utc::now())))

// Deterministic tests select the reference instant.
summarize_member(history, CalendarYear::containing(reference_time))
```

```ts
// Existing MemberIdentity metrics array gets one additional metric.
{
  label: `Declared in ${totals.calendarYear}`,
  value: formatDeclaredTotal(totals.currentYear),
  // Existing count/incomplete presentation remains shared.
}
```

Types and signatures, in existing modules:

```rust
// domain/models/entity_details.rs
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct CalendarYear(i32);

impl CalendarYear {
    pub fn containing(at: DateTime<Utc>) -> Self; // at.year()
    pub fn value(self) -> i32;
    pub fn contains(self, at: DateTime<Utc>) -> bool; // at.year() == self.0
}

pub struct DeclaredGbpTotals {
    pub calendar_year: CalendarYear,
    pub current_year: DeclaredGbpPeriodTotal,
    // Existing current_term_start, current_term, historical unchanged.
}

// domain/services/entity_details.rs
fn summarize_member(history: MemberHistory, year: CalendarYear) -> MemberDetails;
```

Add a third `PeriodAggregate` to the existing traversal. Observe each declaration when its `registered_at` exists and `year.contains(date)`. This shares every currency, precision, completeness, category and count rule with existing periods. Year equality implements the UTC half-open calendar-year interval without constructing boundaries or introducing overflow at the largest supported year.

Wire and consumer changes:

- `inbound/http/handlers/entity_details.rs`: add mandatory numeric `calendar_year` using `CalendarYear::value()` and mandatory `current_year` through existing period conversion.
- `frontend/src/lib/entity-details.ts`: add `calendarYear: number` and `currentYear: DeclaredGbpPeriodTotal`.
- `frontend/src/lib/server/entity-details.ts`: parse the year as an integer and the period through `declaredPeriod`; reject missing fields.
- Existing MemberIdentity caller: append the year metric to the same metrics array, using existing formatting. Use “No declarations recorded” when `declarationCount === 0`; never infer emptiness from null or zero amounts.
- Extend existing service, serialization, parser and view fixtures/tests. Include Dec 31/Jan 1 UTC transitions, following-year exclusion, undated records, unknown categories, missing GBP, foreign currencies, exact decimals and zero.

Alternative: represent the period as `RegistrationRange { start, end }`. That generalizes to arbitrary reporting intervals but exposes two correlated timestamps plus a separate display year. For this single calendar-year feature, `CalendarYear` gives the smaller interface and owns inclusion and labeling together. No repository or database changes are needed.
